WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.302
-Try the chicken.
It's the greatest.

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:05.271
-Uh, it looks spicy.
My stomach.

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:07.340
-Oh, you're missing out, Marty.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:11.510
But then again, I suspect you
miss out on a lot, don't you?

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:15.014
Do you think the goal in life
is to avoid getting hurt?

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:18.017
The goal of life is to live.

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:21.120
Getting hurt is just the price
of admission, my friend.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.156
-We're back with Paul Rudd,
everybody.

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:24.391
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:28.595
So, this is
"The Shrink Next Door."

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:30.462
This is based on a true story.
-Yeah.

00:00:30.462 --> 00:00:31.697
-And it's you and Will Ferrell.

00:00:31.697 --> 00:00:33.866
You guys haven't worked together
since "Anchorman."

00:00:33.866 --> 00:00:36.836
And this is a giant departure.
Which is good,

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:39.038
because it would be very weird
to do something else

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:41.007
in the same tone as "Anchorman."
-Yeah.

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:43.075
As fun as that was.
Yeah, this is a different thing.

00:00:43.075 --> 00:00:46.946
This is a true story.
It was based on --

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:48.848
There was a podcast called
"The Shrink Next Door"

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.383
that came out
a couple years ago

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:53.119
that follows the story of these,
kind of, really, these two guys,

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.554
a therapist and his patient.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:57.623
Will plays the patient,
Marty Markowitz.

00:00:57.623 --> 00:01:01.860
And it kind of tracks them over
the course of about 30 years,

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:06.366
and it's -- he didn't pick
the right therapist.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:08.668
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:10.336
-That becomes apparent
very clear --

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:12.671
very early
in their relationship.

00:01:12.671 --> 00:01:15.441
-Right. Yeah.
So -- But then, over time,

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:16.809
you know, he kind of --

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:19.311
You know, you kind of
get sucked in a little bit,

00:01:19.311 --> 00:01:21.080
and the therapist kind of

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.216
takes over his life
a little bit, yeah.

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:25.185
-Was it nice
to work with Will again?

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:27.020
Obviously, it's been some years.
-The greatest.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:28.788
-Yeah.
-You know him really well.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:31.724
Who's better than that guy?
-Yeah, it's really true.

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:36.195
And I don't mean to blow smoke.
But you guys are very similar

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:38.665
in that when people ask me
what people like you are like,

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:40.399
I'm like, "You can't believe it,
but they're as nice

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:41.501
as you would want them to be."

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.069
-Well, you're very nice
for saying that.

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:46.238
I'm kind of --
I'm pretty awed by the guy.

00:01:46.238 --> 00:01:48.207
And I just think
that it is true.

00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:50.242
He treats people
really, really well.

00:01:50.242 --> 00:01:52.778
And he's so
kind of sweet and talented.

00:01:52.778 --> 00:01:54.313
I loved working with him
on this, too,

00:01:54.313 --> 00:01:56.449
because it's such
a different side of him,

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:59.652
but you really get to see, like,
"Oh, yeah, he's a great actor

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:01.287
in addition
to being a great guy."

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:03.489
So, it was really --
it was a real blast

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:04.790
to work on it with him on it.

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:07.059
-You're also in the new
"Ghostbusters" film.

00:02:07.059 --> 00:02:08.961
Congratulations.
We were talking about stage.

00:02:08.961 --> 00:02:11.397
I had such
an emotional reaction to it,

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:14.600
not just based on how great
the film is, but, like,

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:17.303
seeing "Ghostbusters" as a kid,
I have a real memory of, like,

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:19.338
going to the theater
and seeing that film

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:21.874
and feeling like,
"Oh, this is a kids movie,

00:02:21.874 --> 00:02:23.475
but the people in it are cooler

00:02:23.475 --> 00:02:24.610
than most people
in kids movies."

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:26.045
-Right.
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:28.414
-Which must have made it
so amazing to be asked

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:29.815
to be a part
of the legacy of it.

00:02:29.815 --> 00:02:32.652
-Yeah, for sure.
I mean that was --

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.754
Our generation,
I mean, I remember, too,

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:38.124
when that movie came out,
and it was an event.

00:02:38.124 --> 00:02:41.594
And then, it becomes kind of
part of just the culture,

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:44.964
that Ray Parker Jr. song,
and everything was,

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:48.067
from all angles,
it was just a huge deal.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:50.503
And so now, this is made in --

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:53.873
Jason Reitman wrote it
and directed it.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:56.442
His father, Ivan Reitman,
directed the original.

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:59.145
So, there's this
just lineage that's happening,

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:01.814
and to kind of be a part
of all that is pretty nuts.

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:05.618
-And, you know, trying not
to give anything away,

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:09.722
but we had the original --
the three Ghostbusters

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.757
who are still with us --
Bill and Danny and Ernie.

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:14.560
And it just must have been so
surreal to see them showing up

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:16.729
on set and getting to
not just work them

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:19.132
but see them
in their old bustin' gear.

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:20.633
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:23.035
-It's pretty surreal.
[ Laughs ]

00:03:23.035 --> 00:03:27.106
Pretty surreal to say the least,
for sure, yeah.

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:28.875
-I feel like you --
Every time you're here,

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:30.777
there's things
that you're worried --

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:31.944
that you don't want
to give away spoilers.

00:03:31.944 --> 00:03:33.913
Like, that's one of
the terrifying things

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.080
of being an actor
in the Marvel Universe.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:36.615
-Well, it's like
a weird thing now, isn't it?

00:03:36.615 --> 00:03:39.451
That we're, you know,
all of a sudden,

00:03:39.451 --> 00:03:41.954
there are all these things
you can't talk about

00:03:41.954 --> 00:03:44.156
and things that, yeah,
you don't want to give away.

00:03:44.156 --> 00:03:45.691
I think --
-Yeah, it must be

00:03:45.691 --> 00:03:47.860
especially hard when you go on,
like, a talk show.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:50.863
[ Laughter ]
-Knowing it's gonna be an issue.

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:52.898
Yeah.
It's a minefield.

00:03:52.898 --> 00:03:55.802
-So, you were here, and we were
talking about the things

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:57.336
you can't talk about.
-Mm.

00:03:57.336 --> 00:03:59.472
This is before
they had announced

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:02.775
the title of the Marvel film was
"Avengers: Endgame."

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:04.310
-Mm.
-That was a big announcement.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.012
-Right.
-Which I will say,

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:08.014
I think that's really silly,
because I feel like people

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:09.949
are gonna see those movies,
no matter what the titles are.

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:11.117
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:12.351
-I think you're right.
-I think I'm right.

00:04:12.351 --> 00:04:14.253
-I think that one had
a good shot of -- yeah.

00:04:14.253 --> 00:04:15.888
-Yeah, I mean,
I feel like even it's called

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:17.690
"Avengers:
The Gang's Back Together,"

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:20.359
I think people would've like...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:22.461
I did not know
the title was "Endgame."

00:04:22.461 --> 00:04:24.330
-Right, no one did.
It wasn't announced.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.565
-But then, we were having
a conversation here,

00:04:26.565 --> 00:04:30.003
and I said, "Endgame."
And I want to show the clip,

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:31.937
because I feel like,
in that moment,

00:04:31.937 --> 00:04:34.407
you looked like you're worried
that you accidentally told me.

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:35.541
-"Did I mess up?"
-Yeah.

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:37.577
-Oh.
-Show it real quick.

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:38.944
-I think I messed up.
I think I messed up.

00:04:38.944 --> 00:04:40.146
-You think you messed up.
-Yeah.

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:43.615
-Well, I think...
[ Audience groans, applause ]

00:04:43.615 --> 00:04:45.017
I don't know how
that could mess up, though,

00:04:45.017 --> 00:04:46.385
'cause I would only think
that would make

00:04:46.385 --> 00:04:49.622
more people see the movie,
which I feel like's the endgame.

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:52.158
-You know what? You're right.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:54.627
Oh, there's a pause.
-Yeah!

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:56.496
-Oh, my God!
I think my stomach went, "Ugh!"

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:58.430
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.430 --> 00:04:59.598
-You go back
to the dressing room,

00:04:59.598 --> 00:05:01.567
they're like,
"We have a new Ant-Man."

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.302
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:06.205
"We're using our backup
Ant-Man from here on out."

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:08.407
-"We're gonna
go with Will Ferrell."

00:05:08.407 --> 00:05:10.009
-"We hear
he's lovely to work with, Paul."

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:12.511
-"He's the greatest guy
in show business."

00:05:12.511 --> 00:05:14.079
-Hey, thanks
for being here again, man.

00:05:14.079 --> 00:05:15.581
It's always such a pleasure
to see you.

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.216
Paul Rudd, everybody.
New episodes of

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:18.750
"The Shrink Next Door"
available to stream

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:20.720
Fridays on Apple TV+.

